    "tree_id": "6dd8f54ed80bd4389546e3e4216808ccb5d96780",
    "message": "feat(hvf): synthesize guest data breakpoints for scalar MMIO\n\nEmulated scalar MMIO previously completed without synthesizing the guest\ndata-breakpoint causes the access should raise, so a watched load could\nreturn its value and advance RIP without the required post-access #DB.\nMatch the validated linear byte range against guest DR0-DR3/DR7, retain\nthe resulting causes under the existing pending-I/O exclusion, and let\nhardware deliver #DB after completion.\n\n- Add a four-slot DR0-DR3/DR7 matcher covering local/global enables,\n  read/write conditions and the 1/2/4/8-byte LEN encodings, and reject\n  unsupported access widths.\n- Carry the validated linear address on MMIO plans alongside the device\n  physical address so matching uses the guest-visible range.\n- Stage causes into the serialized pending-debug VMCS field without\n  touching DR6, and fence execution when SDK reads or staging fail.\n- Extend the native consumer with 192 data-debug cases and add an\n  independent Linux KVM control that records 336 observations.\n- Record the qualification bundle, including the baseline failure, the\n  retention-reversal probe and the final owner/portable runs, and note\n  that native HVF execution remains pending exact-source CI.",
    "timestamp": "2026-11-05T22:19:56Z",
